<title>PERU: INTERVIEW - Peru's Cervesur's.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW - Peru's Cervesur's.</headline>
<byline>Marco Aquino</byline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's second largest brewery, Compania Cervecera del Sur,, said it is more likely to issue American Despositary Receipts (ADRs) or bonds than take on a new partner during its current higher-than-expected growth cycle.</p>
<p>The company, a Lima blue-chip, was recently widely rumored to be on the brink of a merger.</p>
<p>But &quot;I was the first to be surprised by that rumor,&quot; general manager Andres Von Wedemeyer told Reuters in an interview. &quot;We are not looking for a strategic partner.&quot;</p>
</text>
